response properties of dorsal cochlear nucleus output neurons: role of inhibitory input</article-title><source>J Neurosci</source><year>2005</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>10952</fpage><lpage>10959</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16306408</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Caspary</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Holder</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name><name><surname>Hughes</surname><given-names>LF</given-names></name><name><surname>Milbrandt</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>McKernan</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Naritoku</surname><given-names>DK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Age-related changes in GABA(A) receptor subunit composition and function in rat auditory system</article-title><source>Neuroscience</source><year>1999</year><volume>93</volume><fpage>307</fpage><lpage>312</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10430494</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chagnac-Amitai</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Connors</surname><given-names>BW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Horizontal spread of synchronized activity in neocortex and its control by GABA-mediated inhibition</article-title><source>J Neurophysiol</source><year>1989</year><volume>61</volume><fpage>747</fpage><lpage>758</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2542471</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cherubini</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Conti</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Generating diversity at GABAergic synapses</article-title><source>Trends Neurosci</source><year>2001</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>